# Copy to .env (repo-root or this directory) and fill in real values.
# Never commit the filled-in .env — .gitignore already excludes .env* except this file.
#
# These four are read by ~38 scripts in this directory. Getting NEO4J_DATABASE wrong
# doesn't fail loudly at startup: the driver connects, then every session(database=...)
# call fails, which the ingest scripts surface as four [WRITE RETRY] lines and a raise.

# --- Current target: self-hosted Neo4j Community Edition on Oracle Always Free ---
# (ADR/migration note: moved off Aura Free's 200k-node cap. See the ACKG migration notes.)
#
# NEO4J_URI     bolt:// for a single instance. neo4j:// asks the driver to do routing /
#               cluster discovery, which a single CE box doesn't serve. Use neo4j+s:// or
#               bolt+s:// ONLY if you configured TLS on the host. Default port 7687.
# NEO4J_DATABASE  MUST be exactly "neo4j". Community Edition serves exactly one database
#               and that is its fixed name — CE has no CREATE DATABASE. Anything else
#               (an instance id, a project name) fails on every query.
NEO4J_URI=bolt://your-neo4j-host:7687
NEO4J_USER=neo4j
NEO4J_PASSWORD=your-password
NEO4J_DATABASE=neo4j

# --- If you ever point these back at Neo4j Aura instead ---
# NEO4J_URI=neo4j+s://your-instance-id.databases.neo4j.io
# NEO4J_USER=neo4j                # not the instance id
# NEO4J_PASSWORD=your-password    # generated once at instance creation
# NEO4J_DATABASE=neo4j            # also "neo4j" on Aura; the instance id lives in the URI

# Aura *account* API credentials — NOT the database password above. Needed only by
# gds_prototype.py (ADR-0009) to provision an ephemeral Aura Graph Analytics session,
# which is an Aura-only feature and is unrelated to the self-hosted instance the rest of
# this toolkit now talks to. Leave blank unless you are running that one script.
# Generate from the Aura Console: account menu (top right) -> "Aura API and Credentials"
# -> Create. The secret is shown once — save it immediately.
AURA_API_CLIENT_ID=your-aura-api-client-id
AURA_API_CLIENT_SECRET=your-aura-api-client-secret
